---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import WedgeRelated from '../../components/WedgeRelated.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../site.config.mjs';
import { aksSafeHarborAnswer } from '../../data/directAnswers';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Whose entity holds the payer contracts and credentialing files?', a: 'In the rental phase, Anvil\'s PC bills, collects, and pays under written agreements with your entity. In the ownership phase, payer contracts, credentialing files, and rates are held by your own PC.' },
  { q: 'What is the Anti-Kickback Statute safe harbor for an MSO in telehealth?', a: aksSafeHarborAnswer },
  { q: 'Is Anvil SOC 2 certified?', a: 'Not yet. SOC 2 Type II is in progress. The trust center will publish the report and sub-processor list on completion. HIPAA program, encryption, access controls, and audit logging are in place today.' },
  { q: 'Will you sign a BAA?', a: 'Yes, as part of onboarding. Request one on the BAA page.' },
  { q: 'Does this website collect PHI?', a: 'No. The marketing site collects business contact information only. Never enter patient information in a form here.' },
];
---
<SubpageLayout
  metaTitle="Credentialing and contract compliance for telehealth"
  title="Credentialing and contract compliance for telehealth"
  description="Credentialing and contract compliance for telehealth: written agreements, fees set in advance, files held by your PC, HIPAA in place, SOC 2 in progress."
  eyebrow="Platform / Compliance"
  prompt="How do credentialing and payer contracts stay compliant as volume moves?"
  promptId="compliance-answer"
  answer="Every engagement runs on written agreements with terms of at least one year, and fees are set in advance, not tied to volume or value of referrals. Counsel reviews every engagement. In the ownership phase, payer contracts, credentialing files, and rates are held by your own PC."
  updated
  sub="Clinicians go live by roster-add under existing contracts, then full enrollment under your own PC, with every file tracked per clinician and per payer."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Platform', path: '/platform' }, { name: 'Compliance', path: '/platform/compliance' }]}
  showCrumbs
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Bring your counsel. We will bring ours."
  ctaBody="We share the structure memo summary and the agreement templates during diligence."
  ctaPrimary={{ label: 'Get started', href: '/contact' }}
  ctaSecondary={{ label: 'Trust center', href: SITE.trustUrl }}
>
  <Section id="credentialing-compliance" eyebrow="Credentialing" title="Credentialing files that follow the contract">
    <p class="lede">Part of Anvil's <a href="/platform">insurance operations platform for care companies</a>, with the other four workstreams.</p>
    <p class="lede">Roster-adds under existing contracts typically take weeks. Full enrollment under your own entity takes longer, so we track every file to the day through <a href="/platform/credentialing">telehealth credentialing services</a>. In the ownership phase, payer contracts, credentialing files, and rates are held by your own PC. That is how you <a href="/own-your-contracts">own your payer contracts</a>.</p>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">How rosters and enrollment hang off a payer contract is covered in <a href="/resources/what-in-network-nationally-means">what in-network nationally means</a>.</p>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">Those files sit inside <a href="/">insurance billing infrastructure for virtual care</a>. Claims under either entity run through <a href="/platform/rcm">Telehealth revenue cycle management (RCM)</a>. Psychiatry, therapy, and ABA panels are <a href="/solutions/behavioral-health">Behavioral health payer contracting for telehealth</a>.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section id="contract-compliance" eyebrow="Contracts" title="Contract terms set in advance" intro="The rental phase runs on written agreements with Anvil's PC. The ownership phase runs on a management services agreement between your MSO and your own PC.">
    <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:24px">Volume later sits on contracts your PC holds, which is how you own your payer contracts. The rent-first choice is <a href="/own-your-contracts#rent-or-build">renting a PC versus building your own professional corporation</a>. If you are leaving a rental vendor, start with <a href="/solutions/switching">switching from a network rental vendor</a>. To compare vendors, see the <a href="/compare/bridge">Bridge alternative fact table</a>. Planning ranges start at <a href="/rates/code/90837">90837 reimbursement rates by state</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Rental phase</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Your entity leases clinicians to Anvil's PC at a fixed, fair-market-value rate</li>
          <li>Your MSO provides administrative services to Anvil's PC for a fixed fee</li>
          <li>Fees set in advance, not tied to volume or value of referrals</li>
          <li>Written agreements with terms of at least one year</li>
          <li>Anvil's PC bills, collects, and pays under those agreements</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted">Structured to align with the personal services and management contracts safe harbor, 42 CFR 1001.952(d). Counsel reviews every engagement. This is a description, not legal advice.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Ownership phase</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Your own PC formed in each state, with the entity type that state requires</li>
          <li>Management services agreement between your MSO and your PC</li>
          <li>Payer contracts, credentialing files, and rates held by your PC</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section eyebrow="Security and privacy" title="What is in place, and what is dated" tight>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>HIPAA privacy and security program, BAA available</td><td>In place</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest</td><td>In place</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Role-based access, MFA, audit logging</td><td>In place</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Annual risk assessment and workforce training</td><td>In place</td></tr>
          <tr><td>SOC 2 Type II</td><td>In progress. Target date publishes with the trust center.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Public trust center and sub-processor list</td><td>On SOC 2 completion</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:12px">Compliance copy is reviewed by counsel before publication.</p>
  </Section>
  <WedgeRelated current="/platform/compliance" />
</SubpageLayout>
